# Copy to .env for local dev. All EXPO_PUBLIC_* vars are inlined into the
# client bundle at build time — see https://docs.expo.dev/guides/environment-variables/

# Nothing here is required for local dev.
#
# Note on EXPO_PUBLIC_USE_RN_FETCH: this used to be set to 1, because the
# image-upload helpers built multipart bodies with React Native's proprietary
# `{ uri, name, type }` FormData shorthand, which expo/fetch rejects. It was
# never set in eas.json, so device builds ran the opposite fetch from local
# dev and uploads failed there with "Network request failed". Uploads now go
# through expo-file-system's native upload (src/api/catalog.ts) and work under
# either implementation, so the flag is gone and both environments run the
# Expo SDK default. Don't reintroduce it without re-checking that file.

# Optional: override the auto-detected dev-machine LAN address, e.g. for
# production/EAS builds that should point at the real API.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.example.com
